                <pb facs="0642" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-09T15:00:00+08:00">March 9, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 9—4:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>317. Following from Reuter, Changchun, March 8th: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The ex-Emperor Hsuan Tung arrived
                            here by special train at 3 p.m. today and was greeted at the station by
                            the Japanese Consul General, General Ma
                                Chan-shan and others, who bowed three times as the
                            ex-Emperor alighted followed by his consort and two other ladies. The
                            ‘Regent Designated’ immediately proceeded to the municipal headquarters,
                            which he is occupying as his residence.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
